This license covers the software, scripts, documentation, models and
other materials in this repository ("the Work").

1. Permission. You may use, copy, run, study and modify the Work, and
   build new work on it, free of charge, subject to the conditions
   below.

2. Share your findings back, for free. If you use the Work or anything
   built from it, you must make your Findings publicly available, free
   of charge, within 90 days of first producing them, and keep them
   available. "Findings" means:
     (a) any changes, fixes or improvements you make to the Work, as
         source code; and
     (b) what you learned from using it: results, backtests, accuracy
         or calibration measurements, and what did and did not work,
         described in enough detail that others could understand and
         check it.
   You can satisfy this by opening an issue or pull request on the
   original repository, or by publishing a public repository or
   write-up and linking to it from an issue on the original
   repository.

3. No selling or paywalling. You may not sell, license for a fee, put
   behind a paywall or subscription, or otherwise charge for the Work,
   anything built from it, or Findings derived from it. Using the Work
   privately for your own research does not by itself break this
   condition, but condition 2 still applies.

4. Credit. Keep this license and the copyright notice with every copy
   or modified version of the Work, and credit "Apex by Demetrius
   Reynolds" with a link to the original repository in your Findings
   and in anything you build from the Work.

5. Same terms. Anything you share that is built from the Work must be
   shared under this same license.

6. Ending. If you break these conditions, your permission under this
   license ends automatically. It is restored if you fix the breach
   within 30 days of becoming aware of it.

7. No warranty. The Work is provided "as is", without warranty of any
   kind. The author is not liable for any loss or damage from using
   it. The Work is research software. It is not betting, financial or
   investment advice, and it does not place bets.

